# 8-Bit Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) using Verilog HDL

## Project Overview

An Arithmetic Logic Unit (ALU) is the core component of a processor that performs arithmetic and logical operations.

This project implements an **8-bit ALU** capable of performing eight different operations selected using a 3-bit control signal.

---

## Features

- 8-bit Data Width
- Arithmetic Operations
- Logical Operations
- Combinational Circuit
- Synthesizable Verilog HDL Design

---

## Inputs

| Signal | Width | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| A | 8 | Operand A |
| B | 8 | Operand B |
| ALU_Sel | 3 | Operation Select |

---

## Outputs

| Signal | Width | Description |
|--------|------|-------------|
| ALU_Out | 8 | Result |
| CarryOut | 1 | Carry/Borrow Flag |

---

## ALU Operations

| ALU_Sel | Operation |
|---------|-----------|
| 000 | Addition (A + B) |
| 001 | Subtraction (A - B) |
| 010 | Bitwise AND |
| 011 | Bitwise OR |
| 100 | Bitwise XOR |
| 101 | Bitwise NOT A |
| 110 | Left Shift A by 1 |
| 111 | Right Shift A by 1 |

---

## Software Required

- Icarus Verilog
- GTKWave
- ModelSim
- Vivado

---

## Compile

iverilog -o alu alu_8bit.v tb_alu_8bit.v

## Run

vvp alu

## View Waveform

gtkwave alu_8bit.vcd

---

## Expected Result

The ALU performs all arithmetic and logical operations correctly based on the selected operation code.